Bundled with them: CPython (PSF-2.0) from python-build-standalone, including
the libraries CPython links (OpenSSL Apache-2.0, libffi MIT, SQLite public
domain, zlib, and others; their licence texts are in
LICENSES/python-build-standalone/), and every Python distribution the locks
list: among them jinja2 and markupsafe (BSD-3-Clause), cryptography (Apache-2.0
OR BSD-3-Clause, with a statically linked OpenSSL), PyYAML, black, jsonschema
and ruamel.yaml (MIT), and pathspec (MPL-2.0, whose Python source files are
in python/lib/ as installed; its sdist is attached to the release with the GPL
sources). Each distribution's licence texts are in LICENSES/<distribution>/.
All are GPL-3.0-compatible.

This npm package is published by ai-swfactory-oss
(https://github.com/ai-swfactory-oss/ansible), which is not affiliated with
Red Hat, the Ansible project or the Python Software Foundation. "Ansible" is a
trademark of Red Hat, Inc. Nothing is modified: the interpreter is the
upstream build and every distribution is installed from the wheel PyPI
publishes. No collections are bundled, and no ansible runtime directory is set:
the caller passes ANSIBLE_HOME. The package is distributed under
GPL-3.0-or-later.
